ypandoc and asserts those exact values.'","'It gates Linux/macOS CI; Windows wheels exist, and a platform without one falls back to identity.'","'Wiki tests never importorskip.'","Runtime identity fallback is defined ('a platform without one falls back to identity'), but the corresponding TEST behavior on that platform is not."],"finding":"The non-skipping pin test hard-imports pypandoc and asserts exact pandoc 3.6.1 / version 1.15 values, and 'Wiki tests never importorskip.' On a supported platform where no pypandoc-binary wheel exists (e.g. BSD), the extra cannot install and the hard-import test errors on collection rather than being skipped, so the full suite cannot go green there. The plan only defines behavior for Linux/macOS CI (gated) and Windows (wheels exist / runtime identity fallback), leaving the no-wheel supported-platform case for the TEST suite unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f04ed792360e471d6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Dependency/CI: 'A non-skipping test hard-imports pypandoc...It gates Linux/macOS CI; Windows wheels exist, and a platform without one falls back to identity. Wiki tests never importorskip.'","norm_id":"ncf52c9280c253158","priority":0.0754,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["BSD developer workstation (supported Platform cell): `uv sync` cannot install pypandoc-binary (no wheel); running `make test` collects the non-skipping wiki pin test which hard-imports pypandoc and errors with ImportError, so the suite fails rather than skipping the wiki lane."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Gate the non-skipping pin test on wiki-extra presence per platform (mirror the runtime identity fallback): where pypandoc cannot install, the wiki test lane is not collected rather than hard-erroring, while still forbidding importorskip on the Linux/macOS lanes it gates.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","c